    "definition": "ἄκρον, ου, τό [neut. of ἄκρος as sb.].\n1. The summit or crest of a hill λ597.\n2. A cape or headland. Of Sunium γ278.\n3. An end or extremity: ἐπ’ ἄκρῳ δῆσε ζυγόν Ε729. Cf.\n   ι328, 382.\n4. The extreme surface: [νύσσης] Ψ339.",
