  "διίστημι": {
    "inflected_forms": [
      "διαστήτην",
      "διέστησαν",
      "διαστάντες",
      "διέσταμεν"
    ],
    "definition": "διίστημι [δι-, δια- (6)]. 3 dual aor. διαστήτην Α6,\n   Π470. 3 pl. διέστησαν Ω718. Nom. pl. masc. pple.\n   διαστάντες Μ86, Ρ391. 1 pl. pf. διέσταμεν Φ436.\n1. In aor. and mid.\n        a. To stand apart or aside: διαστάντες\n       (severing, parting, i.e. in order to form\n       themselves into bodies) Μ86, τὼ [ἵππω] διαστήτην\n       (wheeled apart, i.e. with their hind quarters)\n       Π470, διαστάντες (taking their stand at\n       (regular) intervals) Ρ391, διέστησαν καὶ εἶξαν\n       ἀπήνῃ (stood aside, parted this way and that)\n       Ω718.\n        b. Of the sea, to part, be cleft Ν29.\n        c. To come into variance, quarrel Α6.\n2. In pf., to have one's stand, stand, apart: τίη\n   διέσταμεν; (why do we not come to close quarters ?)\n   Φ436.",
    "headword_normalized": "διιστημι"
  },
  "διί̄φιλος": {
    "inflected_forms": [],
    "definition": "διί̄φιλος [Διί, dat. of Ζεύς + φίλος. Prob. better\n   written thus than Διὶ φίλος. Cf. διιπετής, which is\n   clearly a compound]. Dear to Zeus, favoured by Zeus\n   Α74, 86, Β628, Ζ318, Θ493, 517, Ι168, Κ49, 527,\n   Λ419, 473, 611, Ν674, Π169, Σ203, Χ216, Ω472.",
    "headword_normalized": "διιφιλοσ"
  },
  "δικάζω": {
    "inflected_forms": [
      "δικάσω",
      "δικάσσατε"
    ],
    "definition": "δικάζω [δίκη]. Fut. δικάσω Ψ579. 3 pl. aor. δίκασαν\n   λ547. Imp. pl. δικάσσατε Ψ574.\n1. To pronounce judgment, give a decision Σ506, Ψ574,\n   579: λ547.\n2. To form a decision, come to a resolve Α542, Θ431\n   (lay down the law for ...).\n3. In mid., to seek a judgment or decision, plead one's\n   cause λ545, μ440.",
    "headword_normalized": "δικαζω"
  },
  "δίκαιος": {
    "inflected_forms": [
      "δικαιότατος",
      "δικαιότερος"
    ],
    "definition": "δίκαιος [δίκη].\n1. Conforming to the traditional order of society,\n   observing the usages common to civilized men,\n   civilized ζ120 = ι175 = ν201, θ575.--In superl.\n   δικαιότατος Λ832, Ν6.\n2. Mindful of the usages of courtesy, well-bred γ52.\n3. Acting with due regard to what is right, upright,\n   honourable β282, γ133, ν209.--In comp. δικαιότερος\n   Τ181.\n4. Absol. in neut. δίκαιον, something right or proper:\n   ἐπὶ ῥηθέντι δικαίῳ (when the right word has been\n   spoken) σ414 = υ322.--οὐ δ. with infin., (it is) not\n   right or proper to: ἀτέμβειν υ294, φ312.",
    "headword_normalized": "δικαιοσ"
  },
  "δικαίως": {
    "inflected_forms": [],
    "definition": "δικαίως [adv. fr. prec.]. In due or proper wise ξ90.",
    "headword_normalized": "δικαιωσ"
  },
  "δικασπόλος": {
    "inflected_forms": [],
    "definition": "δικασπόλος [δίκας, acc. pl. of δίκη + -πολος, conn.\n   with πολεύω]. Busied about judgments, administering\n   justice Α238: λ186.",
    "headword_normalized": "δικασπολοσ"
  },
  "δίκη": {
    "inflected_forms": [],
    "definition": "δίκη, ης, ἡ.\n1. Custom, usage, way: βασιλήων δ691. Cf. σ275, τ43.--\n   With notion of privilege: γερόντων ω255.--Applied to\n   a mode of existence or action imposed from without:\n   δμώων ξ59. Cf. λ218.--Something that always happens\n   in specified circumstances τ168.\n2. Right, justice Π388, Τ180: ξ84.--In pl., rules of\n   right, principles of justice: οὐ δίκας εἰδότα οὐδὲ\n   θέμιστας (having no regard for justice or the usages\n   of (civilized) men; see εἴδω (III) (4)) ι215. Cf.\n   γ244.\n3. A judgment or doom: ὃς Λυκίην εἴρυτο δίκῃσιν (by his\n   (impartial) administration of justice) Π542. Cf.\n   Σ508.\n4. A plea of right, a claim: δίκας εἴροντο (were asking\n   questions about their ..., seeking decisions in\n   regard to them) λ570. Cf. Ψ542.",
    "headword_normalized": "δικη"
  },
  "δικλίς": {
    "inflected_forms": [
      "δικλίδας"
    ],
    "definition": "δικλίς, ίδος [δι-, δισ- + κλίνω]. Of gates or  doors,\n   double: πύλας δικλίδας Μ455. Cf. β345, ρ268.",
    "headword_normalized": "δικλισ"
  },
  "δίκτυον": {
    "inflected_forms": [],
    "definition": "δίκτυον, ου, τό. A fishing-net χ386.",
    "headword_normalized": "δικτυον"
  },
  "δῑνεύω": {
    "inflected_forms": [
      "δινεύεσκε"
    ],
    "definition": "δῑνεύω [δίνη]. 3 sing. pa. iterative δινεύεσκε Ω12.\n1. To turn (one's team) this way and that Σ543.\n2. To whirl oneself about, spin round. Of acrobats\n   Σ606: = δ19.--Of a bird, to circle or wheel in\n   flight Ψ875.\n3. To wander, rove, roam Δ541, Ω12: τ67.",
    "headword_normalized": "δινευω"
  },
  "δῑνέω": {
    "inflected_forms": [
      "σόλον",
      "δινηθήτην"
    ],
    "definition": "δῑνέω [as prec.]. (ἀμφι-, ἐπι-.)\n1. To whirl round (before throwing): σόλον Ψ840.--To\n   cause to revolve: μοχλόν ι384, 388.\n2. To whirl oneself about, spin round. Of dancers Σ494.\n3. In pass.\n        a. To go in a circle: πόλιν πέρι δινηθήτην\n       Χ165.\n        b. To wander, rove, roam ι153, π63.\n        c. Of the eyes, to be turned in various\n       directions, wander Ρ680.",
    "headword_normalized": "δινεω"
  },
  "δί̄νη": {
