    "definition": "δῑφάω. To seek for, search for Π747.",
    "headword_normalized": "διφαω"
  },
  "δίφρος": {
    "inflected_forms": [],
    "definition": "δίφρος, ου, ὁ [contr. fr. διφόρος fr. δι-, δισ- +\n   -φορος, φέρω. 'Something that carries two,' i.e. (in\n   war) the ἡνίοχος and the παραιβάτης].\n1.\n        a. A chariot, whether used in war, for racing,\n       for travel or for conveyance in general (hardly\n       to be distinguished from ἅρμα) Γ262, 310, Ε20,\n       Ν392, Ψ335, 370, Ω322, etc.: γ324, 369, 481,\n       483, δ590, ξ280.\n        b. The platform thereof, composed of straps\n       plaited and strained tight Ε727.\n2. A seat (the notion of 'two' app. lost) Γ424, Ζ354,\n   Ω578: δ717, ρ330, τ97, υ259, etc.",
    "headword_normalized": "διφροσ"
  },
  "δίχα": {
    "inflected_forms": [
      "ἔχοντες"
    ],
    "definition": "δίχα [δι-, δίς].\n1. In two: δ. ἑταίρους ἠρίθμεον (into two bodies) κ203,\n   δ. σφισὶ πάντα δέδασται (between them) ο412.\n2. In two ways: δ. σφισὶν ἥνδανε βουλή (they were\n   divided in opinion) Σ510: γ150, βάζομεν (in\n   disagreement, at variance ) γ127.--So of favouring\n   different sides, taking different parts: δ. θυμὸν\n   ἔχοντες Υ32. Cf. Φ386.--Of doubt or hesitation: δ.\n   μερμήριζεν (was in two minds) χ333. Cf. π73, τ524.",
    "headword_normalized": "διχα"
  },
  "διχθά": {
    "inflected_forms": [],
    "definition": "διχθά [as prec.].\n1. = prec. (1) α23 (into two tribes).\n2. = prec. (2). Of doubt, etc. Π435.",
    "headword_normalized": "διχθα"
  },
  "διχθάδιος": {
    "inflected_forms": [
