  "Εἰλείθυια": {
    "inflected_forms": [],
    "definition": "Εἰλείθυια, ης, ἡ [explained as fr. ἐλυθ- (see ἔρχομαι).\n   'The comer,' 'she who comes in the woman's hour of\n   need'; or, 'she who makes the child come forth'].\n   The goddess presiding over child-birth Π187, Τ103:\n   τ188.--In pl. Λ270, Τ119.",
    "headword_normalized": "ειλειθυια"
