    "definition": "ἑλίκωψ, ωπος, ὁ (Ϝελίκωψ) [prob. (Ϝ)ελικ-, ἑλίσσω +\n   ὦπα. 'Throwing the eyes round']. Thus, quick-\n   glancing (as indicating liveliness or vivacity of\n   disposition). Epithet of the Achaeans Α389, Γ190,\n   234, Π569 = Ρ274, Ω402.",
