    ],
    "definition": "ἐρῆμος, η, -ον.\n1. Uninhabited, desolate: νῆσον γ270. Cf. μ351.--\n   Abandoned, empty, vacant: χῶρον Κ520.\n2. Abandoned, forsaken, left to one's own devices: τὰ\n   δ’ ἐρῆμα φοβεῖται Ε140.",
