  },
  "εὐεργεσίη": {
    "inflected_forms": [],
    "definition": "εὐεργεσίη, ης, ἡ [sb. corresponding to two next].\n1. Well-doing, the doing of what is right χ374.\n2. A service done, a benefit conferred χ235.",
    "headword_normalized": "ευεργεσιη"
  },
  "εὐεργής": {
    "inflected_forms": [
      "δίφρου",
      "νηῦς"
    ],
    "definition": "εὐεργής, ές [εὐ- (1)(3) + ἔργω].\n1. Well or skilfully made, constituted or fashioned\n   with art. Epithet of chariots, ships, etc.: δίφρου\n   Ε585, Ν399, Π743, νηῦς Ω396: μ166, π322, νῆα θ567,\n   ι279, λ70, 106, 159, μ305, ο33, ψ234, λώπην ν224.--\n   Of gold, app., fine ι202, ω274.\n2. Done by way of service or benefit. Absol. in neut.\n   pl., services, benefits: χάρις εὐεργέων (for ...)\n   δ695, χ319.",
    "headword_normalized": "ευεργησ"
  },
  "εὐεργός": {
    "inflected_forms": [],
    "definition": "εὐεργός, όν [εὐ- (2) + ἔργω]. Doing what is right, of\n   good walk and conversation λ434 = ο422 = ω202.",
