  "ζόφος": {
    "inflected_forms": [
      "ζόφου",
      "ζόφον"
    ],
    "definition": "ζόφος, ου, ὁ. Darkness, gloom.\n1. The gloom of the nether world: ἀναστήσονται ὑπὸ\n   ζόφου Φ56. Cf. Ψ51: λ57, 155, υ356.--The nether\n   world: Αΐδης ἔλαχε ζόφον Ο191.\n2. The gloom into which the sun appears to set γ335.--\n   The region of darkness, the quarter of the setting\n   sun, the west: σπέος πρὸς ζόφον εἰς Ἔρεβος\n   τετραμμένον (i.e., app., facing west with an\n   internal down ward direction) μ81.--Contrasted with\n   ἠώς κ190. --With ἠώς τ’ ἠέλιός τε Μ240: ι26, ν241.",
    "headword_normalized": "ζοφοσ"
  },
  "ζυγόδεσμον": {
    "inflected_forms": [],
    "definition": "ζυγόδεσμον, τό [ζυγόν + δεσμός]. A yoke-fastening, the\n   rope or thong by which the yoke was secured to the\n   pole Ω270.",
    "headword_normalized": "ζυγοδεσμον"
  },
  "ζυγόν": {
    "inflected_forms": [],
    "definition": "ζυγόν, οῦ, τό [cf. L. jugum, Eng. yoke]. Ablative\n   ζυγόφι(ν) Τ404, Ω576.\n1. A yoke for draught-animals Ε730, 731, Θ543, Π470,\n   Ω268, etc.: γ383, 486 = ο184, δ39.\n2. In pl., oarsmen's benches extending from side to\n   side of a ship: ὑπὸ ζυγὰ δῆσα [ἑτάρους] ι99. Cf.\n   ν21.\n3. The cross-bar which joined the horns of a lyre and\n   to which the strings were fastened Ι187.",
    "headword_normalized": "ζυγον"
  },
  "ζωάγρια": {
    "inflected_forms": [],
    "definition": "ζωάγρια, τά [ζωγρέω. App. orig. the price paid for\n   sparing a prisoner's life]. The price of one's life,\n   a reward for preserving one's life by care or help\n   Σ407: θ462.",
    "headword_normalized": "ζωαγρια"
