  "ἠθεῖος": {
    "inflected_forms": [
      "κεφαλή"
    ],
    "definition": "ἠθεῖος, η. In voc. ἠθεῖε as a form of address to an\n   elder or a master Ζ518 (Paris to Hector), Κ37\n   (Menelaus to Agamemnon), Χ229, 239 (the supposed\n   Deïphobus to Hector).--Sim. in the periphrasis ἠθείη\n   κεφαλή Ψ94 (Achilles to the shade of Patroclus.\n   Patroclus was the senior Λ787).--In ξ147 (ἠθεῖόν μιν\n   καλέω) Eumaeus means that he mentally addresses his\n   absent master as ἠθεῖε.",
    "headword_normalized": "ηθειοσ"
  },
