  "ἰ̄θύ̄ς": {
    "inflected_forms": [
      "ἰθύν"
    ],
    "definition": "ἰ̄θύ̄ς, ἡ [as prec.].\n1. A straight course: ἐπεὶ σφαίρῃ ἀν’ ἰθὺν πειρήσαντο\n   (in throwing straight upwards) θ377.\n2. One's course: ἀΐσσοντος ἀν’ ἰθύν ((steadily)\n   pursuing his course) Φ303.--The course which one may\n   be expected to take: γυναικῶν γνώομεν ἰθύν (how they\n   are inclined, their disposition) π304.\n3. An enterprise, undertaking: πᾶσαν ἐπ’ ἰθύν Ζ79. Cf.\n   δ434.",
    "headword_normalized": "ιθυσ"
  },
  "ἰ̄θύ̆ω": {
    "inflected_forms": [
