    "definition": "ὀρθόκραιρος, η [ὀρθός + κραῖρα = κέρας].\n1. Epithet of oxen, with upright horns Θ231, Σ573:\n   μ348.\n2. Epithet of ships, with sterns running up into a tall\n   ornamental projection (ἄφλαστον, κόρυμβον), with\n   tall sterns Σ3, Τ344.",
